Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A remark on the zeugon (what it means and why it matters).",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " After the breaking exactly one gauge boson stays massless, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "622a6111-b256-4de8-9313-8a1de90c60d9"],
 " for the condensate in the channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K",
     FontFamily->"Helvetica",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fbcc2ed-ed5a-4950-9bf3-325f6d3f61c1"],
 " (in general ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e98f9a0-a1be-488c-abf1-422acda15219"],
 " for a vacuum along ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "88f4d407-ff53-4909-a502-167026fc7cc7"],
 "), the gauge boson of the unbroken charge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641ac8b0-0720-4ec6-963d-fe2c676a033c"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23412f5a-7cfb-4b22-b21d-9edacc2ae03f"],
 ". It is not the photon: only the DiracLike spinor (charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32e9380a-8d74-47f3-a011-0dcad24fca20"],
 "), the bosons ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f850da-a200-4fd3-a287-ff90256e4a34"],
 " and the two non-unitary scalars (charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e765d53-a513-4c99-a3f5-2b9caac36366"],
 ") carry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "501f9ef7-b8af-4b26-ba2a-e6fd41d96a48"],
 ", and nothing in the model carries electric charge. The author, who asked \
for a new massless gauge boson that appears after the breaking and is not the \
photon, offered the solution its naming; the name is the zeugon (from the \
Greek zeugos, a yoked pair), because it is the only gauge boson that attracts \
the two charges of the condensed pair, as the cells above show. Two \
qualifications: its attraction alone would pair the normal vacuum only for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["v",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7b2654b-0baa-49ed-99e7-9403e9e02876"],
 " above about 5.3, almost eight times the coupling of the project, so at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0.7"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ffc213e-5848-4ab5-9f10-faaf5fcda7fc"],
 " it does not by itself hold the condensate, which the pairing term of the \
potential produces; and it is a prediction of the model, not an observation. \
Why it matters: the group that survives the breaking is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "747a4832-fe2a-40aa-86bb-ad2ce2f6963f"],
 ", not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f88823a-3ba2-41aa-9ab3-5e9e695fffb4"],
 "; its second component, a rotation by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Pi]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "94d87592-c9c4-4140-9bff-d197850bc085"],
 " of the isospin combined with the phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "973c7abd-76c9-4f51-9cdb-962035970160"],
 " of the fermion number, is a gauge transformation that reverses the zeugon \
and exchanges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "+"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33472e82-df18-426e-8590-bc39ced5cdfe"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "-"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b71d032b-fd2a-49ae-8986-ccda346b9c06"],
 ", so the charge conjugation of the zeugon is a local symmetry, which it \
never is for the photon. A ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8557ac6d-60bd-462a-96be-0a541e7edaa1"],
 " gauge theory with a local charge conjugation is Alice electrodynamics (J. \
Kiskis 1978; A. S. Schwarz 1982; M. Bucher, H.-K. Lo and J. Preskill 1992): \
the vacua ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "0"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CurlyTheta]"}]], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d22e744a-4f77-4a8f-85de-d816ed337bd4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "0"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[CurlyTheta]", "+", "\[Pi]"}], ")"}]}]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fde1b1c-0d59-49f3-adc0-e831a8a48d1c"],
 " are the same field, so a half-quantum vortex of the superfluid, along \
which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50e81feb-ca90-4dcb-972f-165ebb7bd8ed"],
 " turns into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c09f88d-657c-4875-87fd-b12989a43a7e"],
 " while the phase advances by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Pi]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70713254-beef-4072-95af-587c75e25372"],
 ", is an Alice string, which reverses the charge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12fb9a38-4130-4e25-a598-e317b8fa80d2"],
 " of every particle carried around it (U. Leonhardt and G. E. Volovik \
described its counterpart in a condensate of spin 1 in 2000). These strings, \
and the magnetic monopoles of the zeugon that the sphere of directions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b380f3eb-5cb9-48a7-806c-14f7f7f68a20"],
 " allows, follow from the topology of the vacuum and are not computed in \
this notebook."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25f49d7c-2373-40ae-9db8-5b958eec7841"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part III, first section. The Landau form of the effective potentials: what it \
is, how accurate it is, and why that matters\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"e3f7518a-73a4-4a76-a29e-ee0419effa96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part III of the solution builds the effective Lagrangians ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["CJT",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cde7c9f9-710d-492e-8305-fcbae733776b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["HS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24793f93-4bf9-46a3-a9c6-73bcfd870b39"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["KS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f4afef2-b4a5-49df-b16b-3982f8ae111c"],
 " of the field of the superfluid boson singlet state. Their potential parts \
were summarized by a polynomial, the Landau form, with the remark: \"The \
Landau form is a fit; its largest residual is 0.27-0.7 % of the depth\". The \
author asked (21 November 2026) to explain this remark clearly and completely \
and why it is important, to define the Landau form with examples, and to keep \
the answer in the documents and in this notebook. This chapter is that \
answer. It is the first section of Part III in the notebook; the next chapter \
(Section III.T) is the second, and the other sections of Part III follow in \
the next versions. The computed curves are taken from the Rust program ",
 StyleBox["sf_part3",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (the closed cell of Section III.L.3, with the SHA-256 checksums of its \
data files), and this chapter recomputes from them, by its own least squares, \
every number of the answer; the engine of Part II, which computes such \
states, is used by the next chapter."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a7f66cba-7532-48c0-95dc-3802558f8b34"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.1 The objects", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bd93ba52-edaa-4768-95e2-0f4150e515a6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The field and its effective potential.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The field of the superfluid boson singlet state is the complex isospin \
vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "1"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "2"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "3"}]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "231c6dc3-18d3-4d6a-b41c-0c5a64d7911e"],
 " of the amplitudes of the pair self-energy of a uniform state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P",
      FontFamily->"Helvetica",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", "\[Iota]",
     LimitsPositioning->True], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "\[Iota]"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44f84f49-fed2-4f1b-9830-990505e9dc3e"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K",
     FontFamily->"Helvetica",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10e6cf60-d268-4f46-9fb4-833e0caa1d21"],
 " are the three pair matrices of Part I (",
 StyleBox["kLL[iota]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " in the code) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e37a052d-ac0e-4d19-9b29-13d93fa6abb1"],
 " is one of the five computed methods: HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f840f4c4-41e6-402a-98dc-fde34e4610aa"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83c800e9-1356-40fe-881e-a51e39c5ef39"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ad51eea-4efb-43c7-b77d-a84481565b11"],
 " (the method of Hubbard and Stratonovich with the shares ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["S",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8abf5a84-f3df-4bd0-9c75-fb9327750276"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["V",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a4415231-fbad-4120-8a23-981c1b033d9a"],
 " of the scalar and the vector term decoupled in the density channels), KS \
(Kohn and Sham) and CJT (Cornwall, Jackiw and Tomboulis). The effective \
potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], ")"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e9e2d62-356a-45eb-98ac-59c2fdd7b62d"],
 " is the smallest energy per volume of method ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31167eae-fa15-44c6-a662-0fd6cf3efe4d"],
 " among the uniform states whose field is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1effa1e3-b568-464a-875a-882e4781de24"],
 ", measured from the normal vacuum, so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", "0", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14eb2db4-286f-4e96-8037-00d1e8ae7084"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e2ed69d3-91d0-4dcb-881f-d9ba7419dc59"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How it is computed.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A fixed pair self-energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["a",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53bb201e-c2e1-49e7-bfa5-5c6c09718fe8"],
 ", the applied field of amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2eba2d45-c85b-4341-b53e-76cc5ba286fb"],
 ", is put into the matrix of Bogoliubov and de Gennes, the normal \
self-energy is made self-consistent, and the ground state gives one point: \
its own field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8473d883-e05e-4ada-b5ca-17892080a437"],
 " and its energy per volume. The Rust program computes 61 points per method, \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76b35cdc-5722-4a18-b576-657260158775"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85cffb34-63dd-47ca-925b-4bcb6da466d3"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e7e11a2-2e4c-461f-ba12-fba59ec35367"],
 ", each self-consistent to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "13"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "035c64b1-156a-47ed-8ee2-84e96871c14d"],
 ". Along the ",
 StyleBox["polar",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CurlyTheta]"}]], "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15927aa6-c3df-47a0-aa30-20689d3a70e3"],
 " (real phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CurlyTheta]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c3b5cb8b-8ce2-45dd-b40d-2fa808e30f07"],
 ", real unit vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "625633e7-a385-4c0a-805b-b9ba88fe8da0"],
 ") the potential depends on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalPhi]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d0954e3-b178-4689-aa1c-f628849fdd41"],
 " alone. Its minimum lies at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cab398a2-bd72-4c0c-9c43-b0ba024ec05c"],
 " (the vacuum), and the ",
 StyleBox["depth",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}]}], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "861db0d1-fb14-48f5-bc2e-ca802a3d35e1"],
 " is the energy per volume by which the superfluid lies below the normal \
vacuum. The second derivative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8a6da06-4c9f-4b91-8419-b56086d0d9e2"],
 " of the polar curve at its minimum fixes the mass of the amplitude mode, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b76ee4f-38b4-4c8f-aefd-82544039f596"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4dca5026-0d85-49cf-bef3-17c3e445dfdd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1821ac35-2892-4847-bac0-f28ffe790f76"],
 " are the two coefficients of the kinetic part of the effective Lagrangian."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc13fb34-f38e-4f7a-a856-0275018138bd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.2 The Landau form: definition and examples", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e0b8d86e-36cb-4a3d-a62b-ecbda8509ece"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A Landau form of a potential is its expansion in powers of the order \
parameter (the field that vanishes in the symmetric state and not in the \
broken one) under two rules: only polynomial invariants of the symmetry group \
occur, and the expansion stops after the lowest orders that bound the \
potential from below and produce its minima. L. D. Landau introduced it for \
phase transitions (1937): near a continuous transition the order parameter is \
small, the free energy is assumed to be analytic in it, and the form is its \
Taylor expansion, whose coefficients (the Landau coefficients) are \
derivatives at the symmetric state. The quadratic coefficient changes its \
sign at the transition; the signs of the higher coefficients decide the order \
of the transition and which broken state is the minimum. Examples:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d824c4df-350f-49da-a3f2-99ff142951f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A uniaxial ferromagnet: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "94236b75-7f02-45f4-91cb-2be9beaee940"],
 " for the magnetization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e18b397-c430-4dea-bfb4-e71f3b4484cc"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightArrow]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["mag",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4887291-cf88-4cb0-bb3a-d542e33665fe"],
 "), with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4becb8e3-0251-4169-a6df-1e093ba801b2"],
 " proportional to the temperature minus the Curie temperature and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee551c3b-a582-4bab-b2e8-ac9580c3264c"],
 "; below the Curie temperature the minima are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["mag",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["mag",
            FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a936e632-89b7-4e29-a451-cd157a4a758b"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e4623afb-6165-4072-9b36-1c0186dd522f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The theory of superconductivity of V. L. Ginzburg and L. D. Landau (1950): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f05ddd8f-88c9-483f-b5f9-9caca12b0806"],
 " for the complex pair wave function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
    StyleBox["GL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b6246e-0f6a-4446-993b-eb884cfe9dfc"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c564c99-932a-4690-8840-c47dc64b95e8"],
 "), with gradient terms and the magnetic field added. L. P. Gor'kov (1959) \
derived it from the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer near the \
critical temperature, where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03d2967d-902c-42ae-bec2-2b1adb4c9ff4"],
 " is small; there the coefficients are true Taylor coefficients."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"54e5a0f5-e3d0-417c-a59a-b116dd79d54b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Higgs potential of the Standard Model, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "2"]}], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
          StyleBox["SM",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
       SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c690af7b-e288-43ce-9ebf-afd22d414ec6"],
 ": the doublet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b18a9413-4032-4609-9297-60c67dc7a29e"],
 " has the single invariant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f5acca6d-2e15-46ef-bc5c-8fbde0212701"],
 " of degree 2, and this Landau form is exact at tree level, not a truncation."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"25aa0a16-d8c1-4c46-8efd-0a54c922183e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bose-Einstein condensates of spin 1 (T.-L. Ho, 1998; T. Ohmi and K. \
Machida, 1998), the closest analogue of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47294777-1340-4b88-a477-4604e9cbc62d"],
 ": their order parameter is a complex vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8eaa42ca-ad29-4e47-8899-70569c938bba"],
 ", and their energy per volume ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fe0c5b7-9871-4c74-bd9a-c51c6ac79981"],
 " contains the same two quartic invariants as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b190ab3e-7132-4d05-85ca-3f415ff84bce"],
 ", the second term being the square of the spin. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "253286b5-c22c-41dd-aba0-a84863232af0"],
 " (sodium-23) favors the polar state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73020404-6860-4536-bb83-82f2a817a03f"],
 " (rubidium-87) the ferromagnetic state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Proportional]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0af575c7-2e4d-4199-bdd6-1932ff33a9c6"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8318ef31-f41d-417c-a57c-896c7e612b2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ferroelectric barium titanate (A. F. Devonshire, 1949): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "6"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "758a8445-6294-4ad6-8590-c9013caa1b9a"],
 " for the polarization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["D",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0bd37f60-5793-4f69-b22e-429ad524531d"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ba6a5f5-82fe-4b26-9848-11ae955a7051"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bd53aa7e-bcf2-4ab9-b1ae-ede9ea6bbeef"],
 ": the sixth power is required, and the transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"43f5d8be-f914-4c0c-9f9d-789bf72d0e7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Superfluid helium-3 (A. J. Leggett, 1975): one quadratic and five quartic \
invariants of a complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43f4f34a-e087-46c9-9650-d4acff53ea63"],
 " matrix, whose five coefficients decide between the phases A and B. The \
nematic liquid crystals (P. G. de Gennes, 1971): the traceless symmetric \
tensor of the nematic order admits an invariant of the third degree, so the \
transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1c174367-ead8-481e-8194-be7a3a233922"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The name has nothing to do with the Landau levels of a charge in a magnetic \
field (Section I.6 of this notebook, AS2): the same physicist, another \
subject. ",
 StyleBox["The Landau form of $\\vec\\Phi$.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The symmetry is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f699ba49-6e48-44d1-a7dd-96ed15719d73"],
 ". The independent invariants up to the fourth degree are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "279c2cb0-61c0-4659-8dbf-15e447017372"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6126ddb9-905b-4bfc-b6a5-d6b1252669fe"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05ba0b3f-2181-4867-89f3-6c408137b832"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "*"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "700624b9-103b-47ed-9f00-ad103715c69a"],
 " vanishes exactly on the polar fields. The Landau form used by the solution \
is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16d9bcbd-547d-444c-9a22-f9987bb14bec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[TildeTilde]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "6"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
       "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
       "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], ")"}], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"b21ce44c-81e6-4299-8d99-b795ca2a12ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "the polynomial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["L",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[CapitalPhi]", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "2"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "4"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "6"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c0dfa67-5f18-431d-b1f1-1651f4cde5b1"],
 " along the polar fields. The coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b85591db-caf6-45e0-abcc-e8ae6f5e4927"],
 " is not fitted: it comes from the computed second derivative in a \
non-unitary direction at the minimum, and it is positive in every method (the \
sodium case of the condensates of spin 1). The next cell checks, for random \
vectors, that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "*"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90fd76d6-419e-4caf-87ed-53db257351bd"],
 ", and that it vanishes on polar fields."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3378ceac-20bf-4e39-95f5-89b7ea906769"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"the", " ", "identity"}], " ", "|", "Phi", "|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"^", "4"}], " ", "-"}], " ", "|", 
      RowBox[{"Phi", ".", "Phi"}], "|", 
      RowBox[{"^", "2"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"|", 
      RowBox[{"Phi", " ", "x", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Phi", "^"}], "*"}], "|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], " ", "for", " ", "complex", " ", "3"}], "-", 
       "vectors"}]}]}], ",", " ", "exactly", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"with", " ", "symbolic", " ", "components"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfVec", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"lfRe", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"I", " ", 
          RowBox[{"lfIm", "[", "#", "]"}]}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";"}], "   ", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Phi", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lfRe", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "i", " ", "lfIm", " ", "with", " ", "real", " ", "components", " ", 
        RowBox[{"lfRe", "[", "k", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"lfIm", "[", "k", "]"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfNorm2", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "lfVec", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "lfVec"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfIdentity", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"lfNorm2", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{"lfVec", " ", ".", " ", "lfVec"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "-",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Cross", "[", 
           RowBox[{"lfVec", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "lfVec", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cross", "[", 
          RowBox[{"lfVec", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "lfVec", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"on", " ", "a", " ", "polar", " ", "field", " ", "Phi"}], " ", "=",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"e", "^", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"i", " ", "theta"}], ")"}]}], " ", "r", " ", "n", " ", "with",
       " ", "a", " ", "real", " ", "unit", " ", "vector", " ", "n", " ", 
      "the", " ", "term", " ", "vanishes"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfPolar", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
        RowBox[{"With", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
              RowBox[{"I", " ", "lfTh"}], "]"}], " ", "lfR", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "lfT1", "]"}], " ", 
                RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "lfT2", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "lfT1", "]"}], " ", 
                RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "lfT2", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "lfT1", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
          "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "v", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "v"}], 
             ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
             RowBox[{"v", " ", ".", " ", "v"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], "]"}], 
        "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
